+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""set10: the native measurement of D-031 (a site configuration file the owner changed is kept and named, never
+overwritten by a render) as implemented in commit cd46ca595, on disposable QEMU guests (lab.py).
+
+Two cell kinds, built on set8's and set6's drivers and changing none of their steps.
+
+``set10-debian13`` | ``set10-ubuntu`` | ``set10-arch`` (``Set10Trial`` over ``set8_trial.Set8Trial``): the D-031 code
+installed FRESH (set6's steps: the names pinned first, preflight, origin, install, owner, licence fixture, setup, set1's
+static site). Then, as the logged-in owner and as the owner on the server's shell, sections in this order:
+
+  S0      two PHP sites A ``set10-a.test`` and B ``set10-b.test`` created; every vhost's header, its digest, the ledger
+          row (managed_site_files), the include directory, ``nginx -T``.
+  h-i     a Panel restart with every site unchanged: no write (inode, mtime), no reload, the start line; the file
+          written at creation is the start's text byte for byte (nothing is written at the start).
+  a,b,c,d set8's four owner edits of A's vhost (an added location, a changed template directive, a replaced file, an
+          own include), each with three triggers: Panel start (stopped while editing), restart, General save.
+  keep    "keep mine" through POST /site-config/keep (no identity: 428; with one; the same identity again).
+  take    "take CelikPanel's" on a file the owner set to root:root 0640 (kept at a start first), with its replay.
+  take-stale  the file edited again between the read and the POST: 409 SITE_CONFIG_CHANGED.
+  take-refused  CelikPanel's text refused by ``nginx -t`` because of an owner's file in the include directory: the
+          owner's file put back.
+  e       vhost and link removed: not recreated at start; "missing"; recreate.
+  f       an owner ``.conf`` in the include directory across a start that rewrites A, a General save, a PHP switch.
+  g       A locked (``chattr +i``) while A, B and the static site all need a render: A refused, the other two written
+          with one reload; then unlocked and started again.
+  k       A's vhost replaced by a symlink to the owner's file: classified, refused, not followed.
+  l       deletion of an owner-edited site (a dated copy first) and of an unchanged one; the include directories.
+
+``upd1-<platform>-good`` | ``upd1-<platform>-defective`` (``Set10UpdateTrial`` over ``set6_trial.Set6UpdateTrial``):
+set6's update cells (set5's, with set6's pinning) from the published v0.1.0-alpha.81. Added: before the update, as the
+owner on alpha.81, three sites (R1 created and never restarted, R2 created before a Panel restart, R3 created before it
+and edited by the owner after it); in the good cell a backup of the Panel database (SQLite's online backup) just before
+the update. After the terminal state: the ledger, every vhost, the start lines, the Domains list, the site-config
+state of each site, and the three new POST routes without a request identity (a page loaded before the update). Good
+cell, after its verdicts: the Panel stopped, the backup put back, the Panel started (it migrates again) and read again.
+
+The driver calls only the Panel's HTTP API; every native fact is read over SSH; owner actions and lab preparation on
+the guest are recorded as such. No certificate authority and no licence service is contacted by the driver. Every
+result carries ``native_evidence: false``.
+
+  set10_trial.py plan --cell set10-debian13 --artifacts A.json --work-root /var/tmp/cp-release-drill-X [--dry-run]
+  set10_trial.py run  --cell set10-debian13 --artifacts A.json --work-root /var/tmp/cp-release-drill-X --execute
+"""
